subportal-desktop(1)

# NAME

subportal-desktop - subportal client daemon

# SYNOPSIS

subportal-desktop [*run*]

subportal-desktop *enroll*

subportal-desktop *forget* _NAME-OR-ID_

# DESCRIPTION

*subportal-desktop* runs on the user's desktop machine and connects to enrolled
subportal agents via iroh (peer-to-peer QUIC). It handles requests to open
URLs, transfer files, or show desktop notifications through the local
xdg-desktop-portal D-Bus interface.

# COMMANDS

*run*
	Connect to all enrolled servers and handle requests. This is the
	default command when none is specified.

*enroll*
	Enroll with a server by reading a ticket from stdin. The ticket is
	a JSON object generated by *subportal ticket* on the server.
	After successful enrollment, the server is saved and *subportal-desktop*
	will automatically connect to it on subsequent runs.

	Example:

	```
	ssh myserver subportal ticket | subportal-desktop enroll
	```

*forget* _NAME-OR-ID_
	Remove an enrolled server by name or endpoint ID. The server will
	no longer be connected to on subsequent runs.

# CAPABILITIES

*OpenURI*
	Open a URL in the user's preferred application. A confirmation dialog
	is shown before opening.

*OpenFile*
	Receive a base64-encoded file (up to 5 MB), write it to
	_$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/subportal/_, and open it in the preferred
	application. A confirmation dialog is shown with the file name, size,
	and MIME type.

*Notify*
	Display a desktop notification. No confirmation is required.

# ENVIRONMENT

*XDG_DATA_HOME*
	Base directory for persistent state (keypair, server registry).
	Falls back to _~/.local/share_ if unset.

*XDG_RUNTIME_DIR*
	Base directory for temporary file storage.
	Falls back to _/run/user/<uid>_ if unset.

*RUST_LOG*
	Control log verbosity (e.g. _RUST_LOG=debug_).

# FILES

_$XDG_DATA_HOME/subportal/keypair_
	The client's iroh secret key (32 bytes, mode 0600).

_$XDG_DATA_HOME/subportal/servers.json_
	Registry of enrolled servers.

# SYSTEMD

*subportal-desktop* is typically managed as a systemd user service, started after
*graphical-session.target*. On NixOS or home-manager:

```
services.subportal-desktop.enable = true;
```

# SEE ALSO

*subportal*(1), *xdg-open*(1), *notify-send*(1)

